 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532942,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the missing side and angles in the figure shown.\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5857a141a7727117.png\" alt=\"A ray is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The ray lies in the first quadrant and a vertical dashed line is extended from a point on the ray to meet the x-axis and it makes a right angle. This dashed line measures 6. The horizontal distance from the origin to the line is marked x. The angle made by the ray with the x-axis is marked alpha. The distance from the origin to the point along the ray is labeled 8.3. The angle made by the ray and the dashed line is marked beta.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find <span data-math=\"\\alpha \"></span>.</p>\n<p>The sine of an angle is the opposite side divided by the hypotenuse: <span data-math=\"\\sin \\alpha = \\frac{{{\\text{opp}}}}{{{\\text{hyp}}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sin \\alpha = \\frac{{\\text{6}}}{{8.3}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\alpha = {\\sin ^{ - 1}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\text{6}}}{{8.3}}} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Note: The inverse of the sine function is not 1 divided by the sine function. There is probably a second function associated with the sine key on your calculator. You might be entering something like this: [2<sup>nd</sup>] [sine button] [left parentheses] [6] [÷] [8] [.] [3] [right parentheses] [EXE]</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\alpha \\approx 46.3^\\circ \"></span></p>\n<p>Find <span data-math=\"\\beta \"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since this is a right triangle, you know <span data-math=\"\\alpha \"></span> and <span data-math=\"\\beta \"></span> add up to 90°.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"90{\\text{ }}-{\\text{ }}46.3{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}43.7^\\circ \"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\beta {\\text{ }} \\approx {\\text{ }}43.7^\\circ\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Find <i>x</i>.</p>\n<p>The Pythagorean Theorem states <span data-math=\"{a^2} + {b^2} = {c^2}\"></span> where <i>a</i> and <i>b</i> are two sides (legs) of a right triangle and <i>c</i> is the hypotenuse.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{x^2} + {6^2} = {8.3^2}\"></span></td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{x^2} + 36 = 68.89\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{x^2} = 32.89\"></span></td>\n<td>Subtract.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = \\pm \\sqrt {32.89} \"></span></td>\n<td>Use the Square Root Property.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x \\approx {\\text{ }}5.73\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify. Lengths cannot be negative.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\alpha  = {46.3^ \\circ },\\,\\beta  = {43.7^ \\circ }\">\\alpha  = {46.3^ \\circ },\\,\\beta  = {43.7^ \\circ }</span>, <span data-math=\"x = 5.73\">x = 5.73</span>"
    }
   ],
